WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.508
Hi, I'm Newt!

00:00:02.508 --> 00:00:08.195
MiniCPM5-2B is a small open model with a hundred and thirty-one thousand token window.

00:00:08.195 --> 00:00:10.226
Here's what makes that affordable.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:12.754
It's a stock Llama.

00:00:12.754 --> 00:00:16.216
But its sixteen query heads share just two key-value heads, so the

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:18.236
cache it keeps is eight times smaller.

00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:24.147
Each new token still makes sixteen query heads, in each of forty-two layers.

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:27.615
But only two key and value heads, and those are what get

00:00:27.615 --> 00:00:29.393
cached, for the life of the request.

00:00:29.813 --> 00:00:33.594
Each group of eight query heads reads the same cached key and value.

00:00:33.594 --> 00:00:34.757
The compute doesn't move.

00:00:35.177 --> 00:00:37.883
The memory does: it drops with the KV-head count.

00:00:37.883 --> 00:00:40.589
Eight to one is aggressive, even for this trick.

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:44.124
Here's what one token costs to remember.

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:45.549
Forty-two layers.

00:00:47.591 --> 00:00:48.614
Two KV heads.

00:00:50.443 --> 00:00:52.291
A hundred and twenty-eight numbers each.

00:00:52.907 --> 00:00:55.318
A key and a value, two bytes apiece.

00:00:55.318 --> 00:00:57.428
Forty-three thousand and eight bytes a token.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.008
At the full window that's five point six four gigabytes.

00:01:02.008 --> 00:01:05.537
With sixteen KV heads it would be about forty-five, which fits

00:01:05.537 --> 00:01:06.820
on no consumer card.

00:01:07.983 --> 00:01:09.295
Training came in stages.

00:01:10.572 --> 00:01:14.335
Pretraining stretches the context, up to five hundred and twelve K.

00:01:14.755 --> 00:01:18.441
Mid-training runs at thirty-two K, then a hundred and twenty-eight K.

00:01:18.861 --> 00:01:20.323
Then deep-thinking fine-tuning.

00:01:21.126 --> 00:01:24.976
Reinforcement learning branches that into sixteen expert teachers.

00:01:25.395 --> 00:01:28.814
And on-policy distillation merges them back into one model.

00:01:30.225 --> 00:01:33.083
So the window isn't cheap because the model is small.

00:01:33.083 --> 00:01:36.513
It's cheap because the cache is small, and that's one config field.

00:01:37.983 --> 00:01:42.793
To recap: two KV heads, a small cache, and sixteen teachers distilled into one.

00:01:43.213 --> 00:01:45.184
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:45.184 --> 00:01:45.747
I'm Newt.

00:01:45.747 --> 00:01:46.028
Bye!
